<title>SPAIN: Spanish retail sales fell 1.02 pct y/y in February.</title>
<headline>Spanish retail sales fell 1.02 pct y/y in February.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish retail sales data for February 1997 showed a 1.02 percent fall versus the same month one year ago, and a 19.12 percent fall from January 1997, National Statistics Institute INE said on Friday.</p>
<p>INE gave the following breakdown, February 1997:</p>
<p>		     VS JAN 97     VS FEB 96</p>
<p> General index		-19.12 pct	-1.02 pct</p>
<p> Food			    -4.57 pct	-2.33 pct</p>
<p> Personal goods	     -36.76 pct	 3.91 pct</p>
<p> Household goods	    -18.27 pct	-3.07 pct</p>
<p> Other consumer goods     -29.39 pct	-0.04 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Other consumer goods include toys and personal computers.</p>
<p>In February 1996, Spanish retail sales had fallen a 16.78 percent from the previous month, and 8.95 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
